ProsperoSunshine PS4 port: reconnect recovery (hard reset of retained capture state).

Between Moonlight stream sessions the SceRemotePlay daemon that PBS injects into is
torn down and respawned (observed pid 131 -> 135 across a disconnect/reconnect). The
previous session's retained control context, remote-owner reference and
init/uncertain flags then point at a process that no longer exists, and the
"RemotePlay process replaced; refusing to touch replacement" guard, together with the
teardown_quarantined latch, make that host process refuse every subsequent capture
(begin/init return -1). A freshly loaded host succeeds only because these process-
global values start at zero.

This adds a hard reset that drops all retained ownership/quarantine state without
issuing any remote call, so the next pbs_ps4_capture_begin re-attaches to the current
SceRemotePlay exactly as a fresh host would. The host calls pbs_ps4_capture_reset()
before each open. No behaviour changes for the first session in a process.

--- a/payload/src/platform/ps4/system/control.c
+++ b/payload/src/platform/ps4/system/control.c
@@ -61,6 +61,38 @@
   return failed;
 }
 
+/* ProsperoSunshine PS4 port: reconnect recovery. SceRemotePlay is torn down
+ * and respawned between capture sessions (observed pid 131 -> 135 across a
+ * Moonlight disconnect/reconnect). The retained control context, the
+ * remote_owner reference and the uncertain/init flags from the previous
+ * session then describe a process that no longer exists, yet the "process
+ * replaced; refusing to touch replacement" guard keeps the host quarantined
+ * until it is reloaded. A freshly loaded host succeeds precisely because
+ * these process-global values start at zero; this makes a reconnect start
+ * from the same clean slate. The next pbs_ps4_control() then re-runs
+ * pbs_inject_begin_preferred("SceRemotePlay") and attaches to the current
+ * daemon. Only call this once the previous session's teardown has been
+ * attempted: we are dropping our claim, not reclaiming a live reference. */
+void pbs_ps4_control_reset(FILE *log) {
+  if (log && (initialized || remote_owner_pid || remote_init_uncertain ||
+              capture_request_uncertain || remote_term_uncertain))
+    fprintf(log,
+            "RemotePlay control reset: dropping stale ownership owner=%d epoch=%llu init=%d uncertain(i=%d r=%d t=%d)\n",
+            (int)remote_owner_pid, (unsigned long long)remote_owner_epoch,
+            initialized, remote_init_uncertain, capture_request_uncertain,
+            remote_term_uncertain);
+  pbs_ps4_control_ctx_release();
+  initialized = 0;
+  remote_init_uncertain = 0;
+  capture_request_uncertain = 0;
+  remote_term_uncertain = 0;
+  remote_owner_pid = 0;
+  remote_owner_epoch = 0;
+  /* restore_pending[] is intentionally left alone: the debug gates are kernel
+   * patches that outlive SceRemotePlay's respawn and must still be restored
+   * if this process armed them. */
+}
+
 int pbs_ps4_control_remote_init_pending(void) { return initialized; }
 int pbs_ps4_control_remote_term_uncertain(void) { return remote_term_uncertain; }
 int pbs_ps4_control_ownership_uncertain(void) {
